# Refundable credits and benefits. Read in October 2026 on the CRA's Schedule 6 (5000-S6, and 5005-S6,
# 5009-S6 and 5014-S6 for Quebec, Alberta and Nunavut) and Federal Worksheet (5000-D1) for 2024 and
# 2025, the CRA's indexation page for 2026, Revenu Quebec's Schedules P and B, Finances Quebec's 2026
# parameters, and the CRA's GST/HST credit and Canada child benefit amounts. Schedule 6 for 2026 is
# not published: Quebec, Alberta and Nunavut keep their 2025 values.
#   cwb.single, cwb.couple, cwb.singleParent, cwb.coupleChildren: working income threshold; phase-in rate;
#     maximum; adjusted family net income where the reduction starts; reduction rate
#   cwb.secondaryEarner: the most of the lower earner's working income left out of a couple's family net income
#   fed.medicalSupplement: maximum; minimum earned income; family net income threshold; rate of the medical
#     expenses claimed; reduction rate
#   qc.workPremium: work income excluded, single; couple; ceiling (and reduction threshold), single; couple;
#     rate without children; single parent; couple with children; reduction rate on family income
#   qc.medicalRefund: maximum; minimum work income; family income threshold; rate; reduction rate
#   gstCredit (by base year: paid from July of the next year): adult; child; single supplement; net income
#     where the supplement starts; its rate; family net income threshold; reduction rate
#   ccb (by base year): per child under 6; per child 6 to 17; first and second family net income thresholds;
#     reduction rates between them for 1, 2, 3, 4 or more children; rates above the second, same order
rule tax.cwb.single LIST province
rule tax.cwb.couple LIST province
rule tax.cwb.singleParent LIST province
rule tax.cwb.coupleChildren LIST province
rule tax.cwb.secondaryEarner AMOUNT
rule tax.fed.medicalSupplement LIST
rule tax.qc.workPremium LIST
rule tax.qc.medicalRefund LIST
rule tax.gstCredit LIST
rule tax.ccb LIST

