# OAS recovery tax and alternative minimum tax. Read in October 2026 on the CRA's Federal Worksheet
# (5000-D1), Form T691 and the provincial and territorial 428 forms for 2024 and 2025, ESDC's OAS
# recovery tax page, the Income Tax Act (s. 127.51 and 127.531) and Revenu Quebec's TP-776.42-V.
# The 2026 T691 and 428 forms are not published: provinces and territories keep their 2025 values.
#   oasRecovery: net income threshold; rate (at most the OAS received)
#   amt: rate; basic exemption; share of the non-refundable credits allowed (other than donations); share of
#     the donation credit; share of the partly allowed deductions added back; the gross-up share removed from
#     eligible and from other taxable dividends
#   prov.amt: provincial or territorial additional tax, as a rate of the federal additional tax; rate of the
#     federal minimum tax carryover recovered on the provincial or territorial return
#   qc.amt: rate; basic exemption; share of the credits other than donations; share of the donation credit;
#     share of the partly allowed deductions (the deduction for workers among them) added back
